To minimize overfitting and ensure reproducibility, the following workflow was adopted for each property: 
Feature Screening. All NM-polynomial indices and other descriptors were assessed for multicollinearity using the Variance Inflation Factor (VIF). Predictors with VIF \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
				\usepackage{amsbsy}
				\usepackage{mathrsfs}
				\usepackage{upgreek}
				\setlength{\oddsidemargin}{-69pt}
				\begin{document}$$>10$$\end{document} were iteratively removed until all remaining variables satisfied the threshold, thereby reducing redundancy and stabilizing model coefficients.
Train–Test Split. The dataset of 45 compounds was randomly divided into 36 compounds for training (80%) and 9 compounds for external testing (20%) using a fixed seed (random_state = 42) to ensure reproducibility.
Scaling Within Folds. Predictor variables were standardized to zero mean and unit variance using a StandardScaler. Scaling was fitted on the training subset within each cross-validation fold and applied to the held-out fold or external test set to prevent information leakage.
Model Training. Linear, Ridge, Lasso, and ElasticNet models were trained on the training data. Regularization parameters for Ridge, Lasso, and ElasticNet were selected using cross-validation within the training set.
Internal Validation. Five-fold cross-validation (KFold with shuffle=True and random_state=42) was conducted on the training set. Performance metrics–including Pearson’s R, corrected \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
