We proceed with the following steps to calculate the NM-polynomial indices for the unit structure.
First, we convert the chemical structures of drugs into their corresponding molecular graphs.
To convert a chemical structure into a molecular graph, each atom is considered as a vertex, and each chemical bond is considered as an edge. It is important to note that single, double, or triple bonds are all treated as a single edge. As an illustrative example, we consider the drug Acetaminophen, whose chemical structure and corresponding molecular graph are shown in Figure 9.Figure 9
Chemical structure and molecular graph of Acetaminophen.
