For all nine physicochemical properties considered in this study, the models were trained on 80 % of the data (36 compounds) and tested on the remaining 20 % (9 compounds). The train–test split was performed randomly with a fixed seed (random_state=42) to ensure reproducibility. Unless otherwise stated, all random operations used random_state=42. The following tables (Tables 9–17) report the cross-validation (CV) and external-test metrics for each property. The detailed machine-learning algorithm is provided in the Supplementary Material (Supplementary S2).Table 9
