In Section 6, we examined the predictive capability of NM-polynomial indices in modeling the physicochemical properties of polycyclic drug structures using various regression techniques. The NM-polynomial indices demonstrated substantial associations with several physical attributes. We applied Multiple Linear, Elastic Net, Lasso and Ridge Regression to investigate the relationships between NM-polynomial indices and these attributes. The computed results are presented in Table 9 to Table 17. Furthermore, for each property, we proposed a predictive model and retained only the most statistically significant models for potential use in estimating uncalculated physicochemical attributes. By applying multiple machine learning regression models and validating their performance through both cross-validation and external test sets, we evaluated the strength of the structure–property relationships. The discussion that follows interprets the comparative performance of each model, highlights the key trends observed in the data, and assesses the practical implications of using NM-polynomial indices as molecular descriptors.
