Our results demonstrate higher correlation coefficients between NM polynomial indices and physicochemical properties than those obtained from degree-based, irregularity-based, entropy-based, and previously reported machine learning approaches. Table 25 shows the comparison of different QSPR models with respect to indices, dataset size, and validation strategies. This confirms that NM polynomial indices, combined with rigorous validation strategies, offer a more powerful and generalizable framework for QSPR modeling of drug properties.Table 25
Comparison of different QSPR models with respect to indices, dataset size, and validation strategies.
